  "prompt": "What penalties apply to late filing of a VAT return?",
  "defectClusterTag": null,
  "httpStatus": 200,
  "attempts": 1,
  "responseTimeMs": 18191,
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nPenalties for late filing of a VAT return include a fine of PHP 1,000 and an additional 25% of the tax due for each month of delay, up to a maximum of 50% of the total tax due.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practice, taxpayers should ensure that their VAT returns are filed on time to avoid incurring significant penalties. The combination of a fixed fine and a percentage-based surcharge can lead to substantial financial consequences if returns are filed late. Taxpayers are advised to maintain accurate records and adhere to filing deadlines to mitigate these risks.",
